ABOUT
	The idea is to demonstrate the use of named pipes also called FIFOs

FILES
	fifo-writer.c	Opens and writes into a fifo
	fifo-reader.c	Opens and reads from the fifo
	fifo-re-rw.c    Opens for both reading and writing, done sequentially
	common.h 	The fifo is named here
	fifo2-reader.c  Opens two fifos for reading and writing and does a poll() to check which to read from

RUNNING
   Expt-1:
	mkfifo <PATHANAME> to create the fifo eg ./mkfifo  /tmp/myfifo; sleeptime controls sleep between writes
	./rd <PATHANAME>
	./wr <PATHANAME> [sleeptime]
   Expt-2:
	Independently try out:
	./both
   Expt-3
     mkfifo /tmp/fifo1
	 mkfifo /tmp/fifo2
     ./wr /tmp/fifo1       and     ./wr /tmp/fifo2    on two terminals
	 ./fifo2-reader /tmp/fifo1  /tmp/fifo2  on another terminal


Some experiments:
	1. Change the writer's sleep value (or remove it)
	2. Just for fun see change in behaviour by subsituting 
		the fifo with a normal file
	
